%% alt: Model output passes four checks in order before reaching the user or a downstream system: shape (schema, types, allowed values), grounding (are claims supported by the sources), policy (harmful content, personal data, leakage), and safe handling (encode, parameterise, never execute). A failure at shape, grounding or policy leads to a retry, a fallback, a refusal, or routing to a person.
flowchart TB
  M[Model output]:::model --> S[Shape<br/>schema, types, allowed values]:::control
  S --> G[Grounding<br/>claims supported by sources?]:::control
  G --> P[Policy<br/>harmful content, PII, leakage]:::control
  P --> H[Safe handling<br/>encode, parameterise, never execute]:::control
  H --> D[User or downstream system]:::human
  S & G & P -.->|fail| F[Retry, fall back, refuse,<br/>or route to a person]:::tool
